# 2026-11-22T08:49Z, luminaty. Ranges from the 12-shot smoke calibration; the equality does not depend on the ranges (the run with the real calibration follows the width table).
$ python fpga_network/reference.py --checkpoint <x_step70000.pt> --calibration <smoke>/calibration.json --run w16 --shots 10
the widest possible sum of products, with sign: 40 bits (b1.in); float64 holds 53 exactly, so the torch version computes whole numbers exactly on any shot
run w16 ((16, 16, 16) bits for weights, values, stream), checkpoint step 70000, the first 10 shots of validation_X.npz: integer reference equal to the torch fixed-point logits on 10 of 10 shots (all 12 logits, as whole numbers at 2^-21)
